<title>SPAIN: Santander to take control of Argentine bank.</title>
<headline>Santander to take control of Argentine bank.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's leading bank Banco Santander said on Tuesday it had signed an agreement to take control of Banco Rio de la Plata of Argentina.</p>
<p>Santander said it would give details of the agreement in a joint announcement in Madrid and Buenos Aires at 1400 GMT.  </p>
<p>Santander said it had reached an agreement with Gregorio Perez Companc Sudacia S.A. for the deal.</p>
<p>Santander Investment has long been active in Argentina, but the group has not bought anything in the country in its recent Latin American buying spree.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
